1
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:52,219
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

2
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:54,763
1 YEAR AGO

3
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:02,854
You can sit.

4
00:01:12,698 --> 00:01:13,782
Did you see the personnel changes?

5
00:01:15,117 --> 00:01:16,368
Yes, I did.

6
00:01:16,994 --> 00:01:18,120
How do you feel about it?

7
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:20,497
I'm fine with it.

8
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:22,457
I know that's not true.

9
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:26,003
No, I really am.

10
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:30,090
How are you and Eun-tae?
Are you close?

11
00:01:30,465 --> 00:01:32,301
The assistant manager?

12
00:01:32,384 --> 00:01:33,927
Oh, he's team leader now.

13
00:01:35,012 --> 00:01:36,972
Yes, well, we get along fine.

14
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:39,975
Can you work under him?

15
00:01:41,602 --> 00:01:44,146
Are you sending me to Sales Team 5?

16
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:45,314
Why?

17
00:01:45,397 --> 00:01:48,108
You don't want to work under
a younger team leader?

18
00:01:50,611 --> 00:01:52,154
It's not just about me.

19
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:55,449
I think Mr. Gong
might feel uncomfortable.

20
00:01:56,408 --> 00:01:57,993
I'm asking what you think.

21
00:01:58,785 --> 00:01:59,870
You don't want to transfer?

22
00:02:02,873 --> 00:02:04,416
If I have a choice

23
00:02:05,042 --> 00:02:07,711
I'd like to stay where I am.

24
00:02:11,131 --> 00:02:12,132
Hey.

25
00:02:12,591 --> 00:02:13,592
Yes?

26
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:17,846
I'm telling you to join Team 5
as nicely as I can.

27
00:02:18,388 --> 00:02:20,599
Why do you make me give you an order?

28
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:26,647
I apologize. I'll transfer.

29
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:29,358
- You can go.
- Okay.

30
00:02:33,528 --> 00:02:34,613
Ms. Park.

31
00:02:35,697 --> 00:02:38,867
Don't you also think
he and I aren't a good fit?

32
00:02:41,495 --> 00:02:42,496
Sorry, ma'am.

33
00:02:45,916 --> 00:02:47,626
I wouldn't send you there
if you two weren't a good fit.

34
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:52,381
You and Eun-tae might not know it

35
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:54,883
but you two make a good team.

36
00:02:59,179 --> 00:03:01,723
- Get out.
- Yes, ma'am.

37
00:03:09,398 --> 00:03:12,484
EPISODE 3: WHAT I BELIEVE IN

38
00:03:43,265 --> 00:03:44,474
Aren't you sick of it?

39
00:03:45,684 --> 00:03:46,685
Of what?

40
00:03:46,768 --> 00:03:49,563
Having the same coffee every day
at the same time.

41
00:03:50,439 --> 00:03:54,443
Sometimes, you can have a latte.
Sometimes, you can skip.

42
00:03:54,735 --> 00:03:56,319
But you come here without fail.

43
00:03:57,362 --> 00:03:58,363
It's different every day.

44
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:02,200
I may not be an expert

45
00:04:02,868 --> 00:04:05,120
but the coffee smells different
every day.

46
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:08,749
That's why I look forward
to each cup.

47
00:04:10,041 --> 00:04:12,252
- I'll see you tomorrow.
- Bye.

48
00:04:20,093 --> 00:04:21,470
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

49
00:04:21,887 --> 00:04:23,013
Morning.

50
00:04:34,691 --> 00:04:35,984
Hello, Mr. Gong.

51
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:37,277
You're here early, Gi-tae.

52
00:04:37,527 --> 00:04:38,528
Yes.

53
00:04:49,456 --> 00:04:50,999
I'd like to confirm the meeting time.

54
00:04:52,584 --> 00:04:53,710
- Yes.
- Good morning.

55
00:04:57,464 --> 00:04:58,465
Hello.

56
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:03,470
Great. Thank you.

57
00:05:15,190 --> 00:05:16,608
- Ji-hye.
- Yes?

58
00:05:16,691 --> 00:05:20,779
Can you check the conference room
for our Laknes meeting?

59
00:05:20,862 --> 00:05:22,697
I'd like some extra time
before and after.

60
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:24,658
The meeting is scheduled
for 2 to 4 p.m.

61
00:05:24,741 --> 00:05:27,369
so I extended the reservation
from 1 to 5 p.m.

62
00:05:27,452 --> 00:05:28,495
Is that okay with you?

63
00:05:29,162 --> 00:05:31,206
- You did that already?
- Yes.

64
00:05:31,289 --> 00:05:34,125
Mr. Yang told me
you'd need some extra time.

65
00:05:41,258 --> 00:05:42,968
- Gi-tae?
- Yes, sir?

66
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:44,344
Stop what you're doing

67
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:47,180
and print Alex Cooper's
first-half revenue.

68
00:05:49,307 --> 00:05:50,600
I'm on it right now.

69
00:05:50,684 --> 00:05:52,269
I put him on it already.

70
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:57,816
And here are the malls and outlets
where our brands are sold.

71
00:05:57,899 --> 00:06:00,068
It should help
with your upcoming meeting.

72
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:02,195
Thank you, Mr. Yang.

73
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:04,447
Here you go.

74
00:06:04,823 --> 00:06:06,783
Oh, thanks.

75
00:06:10,871 --> 00:06:12,080
- Ji-hye.
- Yes?

76
00:06:12,163 --> 00:06:15,083
We need two visitor passes
from Support.

77
00:06:15,166 --> 00:06:16,167
Did you...

78
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:18,003
already get them?

79
00:06:19,129 --> 00:06:20,589
Oh, dear...

80
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:24,342
Ms. Lee, can you get them?

81
00:06:24,426 --> 00:06:26,928
I forgot. I'll get them now.

82
00:06:29,598 --> 00:06:31,308
SUPPLEMENT FOR STOMACH LINING

83
00:06:32,934 --> 00:06:34,936
Mr. Gong, have one of these.

84
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:36,229
It's good for you.

85
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:39,316
Thanks. I'll take it later.

86
00:06:39,399 --> 00:06:41,693
No, take it now.

87
00:07:03,632 --> 00:07:05,050
I should've shut him down sooner.

88
00:07:05,133 --> 00:07:07,093
- You liked it?
- Never mind.

89
00:07:11,890 --> 00:07:14,392
They work slower,
so we must be prepared.

90
00:07:17,771 --> 00:07:19,814
- Hello, Mr. Jang.
- Hello.

91
00:07:19,898 --> 00:07:20,899
Hi.

92
00:07:21,066 --> 00:07:22,651
- Oh, I remember.
- Yes.

93
00:07:22,734 --> 00:07:25,153
I'm thinking that's a possibility.

94
00:07:25,612 --> 00:07:28,573
- We should be prepared.
- Sakamoto is...

95
00:07:32,327 --> 00:07:33,328
Hello, sir.

96
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:35,580
What are you two up to?

97
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:40,460
We're preparing
for our meeting with Laknes.

98
00:07:41,169 --> 00:07:42,379
- You two?
- Yes.

99
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:46,716
You... Never mind.

100
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:50,011
So what's the plan?

101
00:07:50,929 --> 00:07:52,764
Why prepare
when we just need their signature?

102
00:07:52,847 --> 00:07:58,019
We thought we should show them
what we can do.

103
00:07:58,103 --> 00:08:00,563
What we're like when we get to work.

104
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:08,780
Don't waste your time.
Just get the deal signed.

105
00:08:09,239 --> 00:08:12,033
Oh, and did you sort out
your other brands?

106
00:08:12,617 --> 00:08:15,537
I'm almost done. I'll wrap up soon.

107
00:08:15,996 --> 00:08:18,540
Why are you taking so long?

108
00:08:18,623 --> 00:08:20,333
- Finish up quickly.
- Yes, sir.

109
00:08:25,255 --> 00:08:27,173
- Then...
- Let's continue.

110
00:08:29,551 --> 00:08:33,596
Was Team 4 told to give up
any of your brands?

111
00:08:33,972 --> 00:08:35,682
We're barely surviving as is.
There's nothing to give up.

112
00:08:36,558 --> 00:08:37,559
Why do you ask?

113
00:08:37,851 --> 00:08:42,355
Ms. Joo asked if Team 4 agreed
to hand over any brands.

114
00:08:42,689 --> 00:08:44,941
Does my team need
to give yours anything?

115
00:08:45,692 --> 00:08:50,155
No, I'm just curious
why people are saying that.

116
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:52,866
- Ju-hui.
- Yes?

117
00:08:53,366 --> 00:08:55,994
Someone from Team 1 or 2
will become associate director, yes?

118
00:08:56,953 --> 00:08:59,039
- Yes.
- Then why is Team 5

119
00:08:59,122 --> 00:09:00,707
giving its brands to Team 1?

120
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:04,586
Because they have
too much on their plate?

121
00:09:06,921 --> 00:09:09,799
Teams 1 and 2 are competing
to get ahead.

122
00:09:10,341 --> 00:09:12,343
And Team 5 suffers in the process.

123
00:09:13,053 --> 00:09:16,222
It's like two thugs
getting into a bar fight

124
00:09:16,306 --> 00:09:19,059
and a civilian gets hit in the head
by a flying bottle.

125
00:09:19,142 --> 00:09:20,268
Got it?

126
00:09:21,102 --> 00:09:23,229
- Yes.
- You didn't get it.

127
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:25,565
And Ms. Joo...

128
00:09:25,899 --> 00:09:27,609
She sided with Team 1.

129
00:09:28,068 --> 00:09:29,444
She thinks Mr. Kim will get promoted.

130
00:09:29,903 --> 00:09:30,904
But my team?

131
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:33,615
No one will get promoted,
and we won't perform that well.

132
00:09:33,698 --> 00:09:35,450
No promotions, no bonuses.

133
00:09:35,825 --> 00:09:40,121
I'm saying,
keep us out of the office politics.

134
00:09:42,332 --> 00:09:44,125
You didn't get that, either.

135
00:09:47,629 --> 00:09:48,963
How did you get in here?

136
00:09:49,881 --> 00:09:50,882
I passed the entrance exam.

137
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:00,767
Are these urgent?

138
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:02,143
Somewhat.

139
00:10:05,105 --> 00:10:06,356
When is the Laknes meeting?

140
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:09,859
It should start soon.

141
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:11,611
What do you want for the brand?

142
00:10:11,694 --> 00:10:13,863
For us to launch it smoothly.

143
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:16,658
- That's it?
- Yes.

144
00:10:16,991 --> 00:10:18,284
That's all I want.

145
00:10:19,327 --> 00:10:22,997
Do you think Gong and Yang
can work together after that fight?

146
00:10:24,499 --> 00:10:25,500
They're boys.

147
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:27,335
They fight, but they make up.

148
00:10:29,546 --> 00:10:34,467
Mr. Jang, whatever the outcome,
this deal will benefit the company.

149
00:10:34,551 --> 00:10:37,887
But I'm not sure
if it'll benefit you too.

150
00:11:07,584 --> 00:11:08,960
- Here you go.
- Thanks.

151
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:10,503
Everything looks good.

152
00:11:11,963 --> 00:11:13,131
Thank you.

153
00:11:19,429 --> 00:11:21,472
Perfect spacing
between the words and lines.

154
00:11:21,556 --> 00:11:23,183
WELCOME TO HONGSUNG
LAKNES ASIA KIM HYEONG-CHAN, SAKAMOTO

155
00:11:54,881 --> 00:11:56,216
I'm Team Leader Gong Eun-tae.

156
00:11:56,758 --> 00:11:58,718
It's a pleasure to meet you.
I'm Team Leader Gong Eun-tae.

157
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:01,596
I'm Assistant Manager Yang Jun-ho
from Sales Team 5.

158
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:04,766
I'm Assistant Manager Yang Jun-ho
from Sales Team 5.

159
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:08,353
I'm Kim Hyeong-chan,
Director of Asia for Laknes.

160
00:12:09,395 --> 00:12:10,605
Hello, nice to meet you.

161
00:12:10,688 --> 00:12:14,067
I'm Sakamoto.
I oversee the Asian market.

162
00:12:14,901 --> 00:12:16,569
- Shall we?
- Yes.

163
00:12:19,697 --> 00:12:21,491
We have pretty good coffee here.

164
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:23,368
- I hope you like it.
- Great, thank you.

165
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:24,702
When did you arrive?

166
00:12:24,786 --> 00:12:25,995
We arrived yesterday.

167
00:12:26,079 --> 00:12:27,580
I see. You flew in yesterday.

168
00:12:27,664 --> 00:12:33,753
If you don't mind, may I tape
the meeting for our records?

169
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:36,673
- Sure.
- Thank you.

170
00:12:45,932 --> 00:12:50,270
<i>I need you to do something for me
before the Laknes meeting.</i>

171
00:12:51,229 --> 00:12:54,941
<i>Ji-hye, find out what you can
about Kim Hyeong-chan and Sakamoto.</i>

172
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:59,028
<i>Their past tells you who they are.</i>

173
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:07,537
I'd like to know how a Korean
became Director of Asia.

174
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:09,914
As a fellow Korean,
it makes me proud.

175
00:13:10,290 --> 00:13:12,417
I studied fashion design in Spain.

176
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:16,129
I was lucky enough
to start as a VMD at Zara.

177
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:20,425
I did that for about three years
before moving to Philipp Plein.

178
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:24,470
Oh, I think I heard
about a Korean working there.

179
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:26,723
That's when I met Ms. Park Hyeon-suk.

180
00:13:27,515 --> 00:13:32,603
Then I started my own business,
but it didn't work out.

181
00:13:33,688 --> 00:13:36,858
That's when I joined Laknes.

182
00:13:39,110 --> 00:13:41,612
We could learn a lot from you.

183
00:13:41,696 --> 00:13:44,198
Not at all.
I'm sure you're both very capable.

184
00:13:44,907 --> 00:13:49,203
<i>Gi-tae, list questions we can use
to gain the upper hand.</i>

185
00:13:49,704 --> 00:13:52,165
<i>In negotiations, questions are power.</i>

186
00:13:52,248 --> 00:13:54,876
WOULD YOU CONSIDER HIRING HONGSUNG
STAFF WHEN ESTABLISHING A DESIGN LAB?

187
00:13:54,959 --> 00:13:57,879
Laknes is doing well in Japan, right?

188
00:13:57,962 --> 00:14:03,509
Japan runs its own promotions
to support the brand.

189
00:14:03,593 --> 00:14:07,221
Does the head office provide
a separate promotional budget?

190
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:16,314
We get 3% of the order value
to spend on promotions.

191
00:14:16,647 --> 00:14:18,191
As much as 3%?

192
00:14:18,649 --> 00:14:20,318
Wow, that's a lot.

193
00:14:20,777 --> 00:14:23,821
What margin did you offer
the Japanese market?

194
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:28,826
Leather goods at 70%,
and apparel at 75%.

195
00:14:29,452 --> 00:14:34,040
Is it true that you offered us
60% for leather and 65% for apparel?

196
00:14:35,375 --> 00:14:38,544
I believe we've settled
the baseline margin.

197
00:14:39,212 --> 00:14:41,464
Isn't there always
room for negotiation?

198
00:14:41,547 --> 00:14:45,301
The truth is,
we were headed for Japan.

199
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:51,099
We called Ms. Park to say hello,
and she arranged this meeting.

200
00:14:51,516 --> 00:14:54,811
Yes, we know
we requested this meeting.

201
00:14:56,813 --> 00:14:57,939
I'll be honest.

202
00:14:59,315 --> 00:15:01,943
We're especially wary
because Korea failed us once before.

203
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:05,738
We're already doing just fine
in Japan

204
00:15:06,114 --> 00:15:08,991
so we're not sure
why we should enter Korea again.

205
00:15:11,077 --> 00:15:14,372
<i>I'll go through Laknes's
last five financial statements.</i>

206
00:15:18,084 --> 00:15:20,128
<i>The answer is in the numbers.</i>

207
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:26,467
The purchasing patterns
and recent changes.

208
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:33,307
To be frank, we were hesitant too.

209
00:15:34,434 --> 00:15:39,147
We do all the work to improve
brand awareness, and the deal ends.

210
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:43,734
I know many brands switched partners
for a higher baseline margin.

211
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:46,070
I'm not saying that's wrong.

212
00:15:46,487 --> 00:15:48,197
I'm saying we take on that risk.

213
00:15:52,743 --> 00:15:57,498
You can give 3% of total sales
as a staff incentive.

214
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:02,879
That's their livelihood,
so that's a given.

215
00:16:03,421 --> 00:16:05,256
Could you reconsider the margin?

216
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:08,426
A 65% apparel margin puts you
between Pinster and Mareige.

217
00:16:08,509 --> 00:16:10,678
But Laknes is
nothing like those brands.

218
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:13,639
Are you aware we take back
all the dead stock?

219
00:16:13,723 --> 00:16:15,600
Yes, that's actually
more work for us.

220
00:16:15,892 --> 00:16:18,561
We have to pick up everything
and send it back to France.

221
00:16:18,644 --> 00:16:20,980
The only one who profits
is the logistics company.

222
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:23,149
How about after the launch

223
00:16:23,608 --> 00:16:26,360
we provide enough product
to stock the outlet stores too?

224
00:16:26,736 --> 00:16:28,029
Would that work?

225
00:16:28,112 --> 00:16:32,241
No, we'll handle the malls
and outlets from the start.

226
00:16:33,034 --> 00:16:36,746
In return, give us the same
70% and 75% margins as Japan.

227
00:16:45,379 --> 00:16:46,380
I'm sorry.

228
00:16:47,256 --> 00:16:48,549
I can't do that.

229
00:17:03,898 --> 00:17:05,566
Hey, how do you think it went?

230
00:17:06,776 --> 00:17:08,653
I think it went badly.

231
00:17:10,446 --> 00:17:11,572
Darn it.

232
00:17:27,463 --> 00:17:29,465
Did you see the look
in Sakamoto's eyes?

233
00:17:29,549 --> 00:17:31,592
- No.
- It was bad.

234
00:17:40,893 --> 00:17:42,270
How did it go, Mr. Gong?

235
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:45,565
- Mr. Yang?
- Let's go upstairs.

236
00:17:45,648 --> 00:17:47,858
- Okay.
- Be quick.

237
00:17:52,697 --> 00:17:54,490
- Gi-tae.
- Yes?

238
00:17:54,949 --> 00:17:56,158
Do you have plans later?

239
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:57,910
No.

240
00:17:58,661 --> 00:17:59,662
Ji-hye, you?

241
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:02,164
I'm free too.

242
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,083
Are you?

243
00:18:04,625 --> 00:18:05,876
Then shall we go out...

244
00:18:07,044 --> 00:18:08,045
No.

245
00:18:08,879 --> 00:18:09,880
- What?
- What?

246
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:12,466
Forget it. It's no big deal.

247
00:18:14,969 --> 00:18:16,304
Did the deal go okay?

248
00:18:19,181 --> 00:18:21,183
What happened? Yes or no?

249
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:25,896
Why won't either of you say anything?

250
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:29,317
Did they sign the deal?

251
00:18:30,359 --> 00:18:31,611
- Mr. Gong.
- What happened?

252
00:18:32,612 --> 00:18:33,946
Let's get a drink later.

253
00:18:36,616 --> 00:18:37,825
Forget the drinks.

254
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:41,829
- Mr. Yang!
- Mr. Yang? Mr. Gong?

255
00:18:43,623 --> 00:18:46,334
We got 65% for leather,
70% for apparel.

256
00:18:46,584 --> 00:18:50,129
We increased the margins by 5%
with a separate incentive clause.

257
00:18:52,923 --> 00:18:55,009
- Good job.
- Thank you.

258
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:58,220
I owe it to you
for letting us do our jobs.

259
00:18:58,512 --> 00:19:01,307
Also, Mr. Yang played a huge role.

260
00:19:03,392 --> 00:19:06,062
These are the brands
that grew under our management.

261
00:19:06,479 --> 00:19:09,690
They all grew by over 50%
from the previous year.

262
00:19:17,114 --> 00:19:19,909
We're not asking for a higher margin
without reason.

263
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:23,537
We're asking you to recognize
the value of our work.

264
00:19:24,538 --> 00:19:28,459
We can deliver better results
than anyone else.

265
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:32,963
The document you're reading
proves that.

266
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:44,016
What does the Korean market
mean to Laknes?

267
00:19:46,644 --> 00:19:48,813
It's a stepping stone to China

268
00:19:48,896 --> 00:19:51,982
so you don't lose anything
as long as you make a decent profit.

269
00:19:53,442 --> 00:19:55,653
That's why your brand
ended up with our team.

270
00:19:56,612 --> 00:19:58,447
We're the weakest team.

271
00:19:58,989 --> 00:20:02,993
They expect us to do an average job
and give you what you want.

272
00:20:04,078 --> 00:20:09,208
You two expected to come here,
sign the deal, and move on.

273
00:20:09,291 --> 00:20:10,292
Am I wrong?

274
00:20:13,587 --> 00:20:15,131
No, I won't deny that.

275
00:20:15,423 --> 00:20:17,550
I'm sorry, but we have
no intention of doing that.

276
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:20,553
To you, Korea might be
just a stepping stone

277
00:20:20,636 --> 00:20:23,639
but to us, Laknes is a brand
we must build and grow.

278
00:20:24,473 --> 00:20:27,101
We don't want to settle
for an average profit.

279
00:20:28,394 --> 00:20:30,062
Adjust the margin.

280
00:20:30,396 --> 00:20:31,897
You'll make much more.

281
00:20:33,649 --> 00:20:35,776
Are you that confident?

282
00:20:38,154 --> 00:20:39,363
You saw the numbers.

283
00:20:46,537 --> 00:20:47,913
Good job.

284
00:20:50,291 --> 00:20:51,500
You deserve a team dinner.

285
00:20:53,377 --> 00:20:54,628
Put it on this card.

286
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:56,213
Thank you.

287
00:20:57,006 --> 00:20:58,007
Mr. Gong.

288
00:20:58,716 --> 00:21:01,177
Did you consider which brands
to give Team 1?

289
00:21:01,552 --> 00:21:03,262
Yes, I did.

290
00:21:03,721 --> 00:21:04,722
<i>Mr. Yang.</i>

291
00:21:05,556 --> 00:21:07,433
Do you want to shake things up
with me?

292
00:21:09,226 --> 00:21:10,895
You're making me feel uneasy.

293
00:21:12,229 --> 00:21:13,981
I'm going to turn
this company around.

294
00:21:17,735 --> 00:21:19,403
We'll keep them all.

295
00:21:21,655 --> 00:21:23,949
What do you mean
you'll keep them all?

296
00:21:24,492 --> 00:21:25,826
We keep all our brands?

297
00:21:27,411 --> 00:21:29,371
What happens then?

298
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:31,415
Who knows?

299
00:21:32,541 --> 00:21:34,001
That's why I said, "shake things up."

300
00:21:34,710 --> 00:21:36,003
What are you saying?

301
00:21:36,378 --> 00:21:38,214
- You can't do all...
- Let him talk.

302
00:21:39,173 --> 00:21:40,591
Aren't you being too ambitious?

303
00:21:40,841 --> 00:21:42,051
You lack the manpower.

304
00:21:42,426 --> 00:21:46,222
That's why I'd appreciate it
if you gave us some extra help.

305
00:21:46,931 --> 00:21:48,808
Then can you handle it all?

306
00:21:48,891 --> 00:21:49,892
Yes, we can.

307
00:21:50,351 --> 00:21:52,186
I've already assigned the tasks.

308
00:21:52,436 --> 00:21:54,104
I think it's doable.

309
00:21:56,857 --> 00:21:58,651
<i>Will Mr. Jang be okay with that?</i>

310
00:21:58,901 --> 00:22:00,945
I can see his furious expression.

311
00:22:01,779 --> 00:22:04,406
That's for me to handle
as team leader.

312
00:22:08,452 --> 00:22:11,747
I don't know anything
about office politics.

313
00:22:12,122 --> 00:22:16,418
I just don't want someone else
to benefit from my hard work.

314
00:22:17,753 --> 00:22:19,630
You know nothing
about office politics?

315
00:22:19,713 --> 00:22:22,258
Politics and I don't mix.

316
00:22:26,595 --> 00:22:27,805
Let's do it, then.

317
00:22:30,683 --> 00:22:32,142
Sales Team 2.

318
00:22:33,519 --> 00:22:34,520
Yes.

319
00:22:34,979 --> 00:22:35,980
Mr. Son?

320
00:22:36,814 --> 00:22:38,691
Okay, I'll pass it on.

321
00:22:40,234 --> 00:22:41,277
What is it?

322
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:43,946
- A team leader meeting.
- Right now?

323
00:22:44,029 --> 00:22:45,030
Okay.

324
00:22:45,948 --> 00:22:47,867
- You have a meeting, Mr. Jeong.
- With whom?

325
00:22:47,950 --> 00:22:50,035
- Ms. Park.
- Darn it.

326
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:53,747
This is just stupid.

327
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:04,425
- Mr. Yang.
<i>- Is it done yet?</i>

328
00:23:04,508 --> 00:23:07,386
We're almost done.
How far did you get?

329
00:23:07,469 --> 00:23:09,430
- It's printing now.
- We're printing it now.

330
00:23:09,513 --> 00:23:11,849
<i>- Hurry up.</i>
- We'll be right down.

331
00:23:18,022 --> 00:23:20,274
Ji-hye, mine will be printed first.

332
00:23:28,490 --> 00:23:29,825
Here's what you asked for.

333
00:23:29,909 --> 00:23:31,327
This covers each team's brands

334
00:23:31,410 --> 00:23:33,495
and this includes the sales figures.

335
00:23:33,579 --> 00:23:36,081
This is each team's current schedule.

336
00:23:37,666 --> 00:23:40,377
- Good job, both of you.
- Will they be okay with this?

337
00:23:40,711 --> 00:23:42,796
Mr. Jang looked sour.

338
00:23:43,255 --> 00:23:46,050
There's no going back now.
It can't be helped.

339
00:23:48,802 --> 00:23:50,763
- Good luck, sir.
- Good luck, Mr. Gong.

340
00:23:52,014 --> 00:23:56,477
It's almost time to clock out,
so I'll keep this short.

341
00:23:56,977 --> 00:23:57,978
Okay.

342
00:23:58,812 --> 00:24:02,691
Sales Team 5 took on Laknes,
a brand no one else wanted

343
00:24:02,775 --> 00:24:04,777
and signed the deal in our favor.

344
00:24:06,028 --> 00:24:07,237
Let's give them a hand.

345
00:24:12,952 --> 00:24:18,374
The original plan was for them
to hand a few brands to Team 1.

346
00:24:19,124 --> 00:24:21,043
But Mr. Gong changed his mind.

347
00:24:22,753 --> 00:24:24,338
He'll keep them all.

348
00:24:25,798 --> 00:24:29,426
I called you all here
to praise him publicly.

349
00:24:30,678 --> 00:24:32,721
Mr. Gong, what's your reasoning?

350
00:24:38,811 --> 00:24:41,522
I thought that was why
my team was created.

351
00:24:42,314 --> 00:24:43,857
Sales Team 1 is a core team

352
00:24:44,441 --> 00:24:48,821
that handles 30%
of our division's total sales.

353
00:24:49,238 --> 00:24:51,782
I shouldn't burden them with brands

354
00:24:52,032 --> 00:24:54,243
that are only starting
to turn a profit.

355
00:24:55,786 --> 00:24:56,954
I'd like our team

356
00:24:57,788 --> 00:24:59,248
to handle its own business.

357
00:25:02,710 --> 00:25:05,254
Mr. Son, what do you think?

358
00:25:06,380 --> 00:25:07,631
I respect him.

359
00:25:08,966 --> 00:25:12,636
I didn't think the youngest
team leader had that kind of idea.

360
00:25:13,095 --> 00:25:14,471
- You respect him?
- Yes.

361
00:25:14,972 --> 00:25:16,849
Shouldn't you be ashamed of yourself?

362
00:25:19,893 --> 00:25:22,229
- Mr. Kim.
- Yes, ma'am.

363
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:24,231
What do you think?

364
00:25:26,650 --> 00:25:27,651
I'm ashamed.

365
00:25:28,444 --> 00:25:30,446
- Are you?
- Yes.

366
00:25:31,405 --> 00:25:33,323
- Ms. Joo.
- Yes, ma'am.

367
00:25:34,324 --> 00:25:37,536
I hear you're still bullying brands
into giving you their new products.

368
00:25:37,953 --> 00:25:38,954
Is that true?

369
00:25:42,207 --> 00:25:43,542
You should know better.

370
00:25:46,170 --> 00:25:48,130
- What about you, Mr. Jeong?
- Yes?

371
00:25:48,922 --> 00:25:51,717
I'm embarrassed as well.

372
00:25:52,760 --> 00:25:55,179
The other team leaders
are competing to get ahead.

373
00:25:55,637 --> 00:26:00,309
Have you decided to do nothing
since you won't get promoted, anyway?

374
00:26:01,894 --> 00:26:03,020
That's not it.

375
00:26:06,148 --> 00:26:07,191
Guys.

376
00:26:07,649 --> 00:26:08,859
- Yes?
- Yes?

377
00:26:10,736 --> 00:26:12,821
No one will say it out loud

378
00:26:13,697 --> 00:26:16,158
but you all know
why Laknes went to Team 5

379
00:26:16,533 --> 00:26:19,119
why Team 5 was supposed
to give its brands to Team 1

380
00:26:19,203 --> 00:26:21,121
and who will be promoted
to associate director.

381
00:26:21,205 --> 00:26:24,124
You're all playing chess
in your heads.

382
00:26:25,584 --> 00:26:28,587
You all think you're so smart.

383
00:26:30,964 --> 00:26:31,965
Mr. Jang.

384
00:26:32,633 --> 00:26:33,634
Yes, ma'am.

385
00:26:33,926 --> 00:26:35,844
Jang Hyang-eun returns from China.

386
00:26:36,178 --> 00:26:37,846
Yes, she'll be back next week.

387
00:26:38,722 --> 00:26:39,807
Send her to Team 5.

388
00:26:41,975 --> 00:26:42,976
Yes, ma'am.

389
00:26:44,895 --> 00:26:46,647
Make yourselves useful.

390
00:26:47,648 --> 00:26:49,316
Don't just scheme.

391
00:26:49,983 --> 00:26:50,984
Do some work.

392
00:26:56,448 --> 00:26:57,533
Bye, ma'am.

393
00:27:07,251 --> 00:27:08,544
Everyone leave
except for Gong Eun-tae.

394
00:27:18,554 --> 00:27:20,055
TEAM LEADER GONG EUN-TAE

395
00:27:34,403 --> 00:27:36,905
Mr. Jeong, where's Mr. Gong?

396
00:27:36,989 --> 00:27:40,200
He'll need some time
to clean up the mess he made.

397
00:27:40,284 --> 00:27:41,410
You can go home.

398
00:27:45,205 --> 00:27:46,206
Go home.

399
00:27:56,884 --> 00:27:57,968
Why did you do it?

400
00:28:03,515 --> 00:28:05,017
Why won't you answer me?

401
00:28:07,186 --> 00:28:09,813
Why didn't you do as I said?

402
00:28:13,108 --> 00:28:15,360
I did as you said.

403
00:28:16,862 --> 00:28:18,697
You told me to take on Laknes,
so I did.

404
00:28:19,156 --> 00:28:21,575
And I listed up the brands
to give to Team 1.

405
00:28:22,743 --> 00:28:26,872
But then I thought I could do it all
with one extra teammate.

406
00:28:27,289 --> 00:28:29,541
Can't I at least ask for that?

407
00:28:33,545 --> 00:28:35,380
What's gotten into you?

408
00:28:36,131 --> 00:28:39,176
Why are you talking back
like you have nothing to lose?

409
00:28:40,135 --> 00:28:42,638
You don't know your place
now that you're a team leader?

410
00:28:43,430 --> 00:28:44,431
That's not it.

411
00:28:45,265 --> 00:28:49,061
Now that I'm a team leader,
I know what the job entails.

412
00:28:52,314 --> 00:28:57,277
Gosh, you're talking like
you've lost a few screws.

413
00:28:57,611 --> 00:28:59,404
Okay, then.

414
00:29:00,906 --> 00:29:03,367
Do you think team leaders
have a fixed job description?

415
00:29:03,450 --> 00:29:04,993
Who decided that?

416
00:29:06,620 --> 00:29:07,663
Gong Eun-tae.

417
00:29:08,455 --> 00:29:10,707
Team leaders,
associate directors, and directors...

418
00:29:10,791 --> 00:29:14,544
They're all people
who do as they're told.

419
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:18,173
If you can't do that,
just start your own business.

420
00:29:19,675 --> 00:29:21,009
This company

421
00:29:21,718 --> 00:29:23,428
isn't yours, is it?

422
00:29:23,720 --> 00:29:24,721
You bastard!

423
00:29:25,264 --> 00:29:27,516
I can't believe what I'm hearing.

424
00:29:27,849 --> 00:29:28,850
Mr. Jang.

425
00:29:30,477 --> 00:29:31,812
In my first year here

426
00:29:32,187 --> 00:29:37,192
do you remember taking clueless me
to Paris to sign a deal?

427
00:29:37,276 --> 00:29:38,735
What about it?

428
00:29:39,236 --> 00:29:41,238
We took a red-eye on Saturday.

429
00:29:42,114 --> 00:29:43,740
We worked all weekend

430
00:29:43,824 --> 00:29:45,909
and went straight to another meeting
when we landed Tuesday.

431
00:29:47,286 --> 00:29:49,204
I did that for just one week

432
00:29:49,830 --> 00:29:54,501
but you'd been doing that
for the whole month.

433
00:29:57,671 --> 00:29:58,964
Sure, we were busy.

434
00:29:59,047 --> 00:30:02,050
We couldn't send anyone else.
So what?

435
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:05,012
You did that

436
00:30:05,887 --> 00:30:08,223
because, like me now,
you were the youngest team leader.

437
00:30:08,849 --> 00:30:11,101
You worked that hard

438
00:30:11,685 --> 00:30:14,062
because you didn't want
your team to suffer

439
00:30:14,146 --> 00:30:16,106
for having the youngest team leader.

440
00:30:17,024 --> 00:30:18,442
Thanks to your sacrifice

441
00:30:18,525 --> 00:30:20,777
we were able to keep our heads down
and work hard.

442
00:30:24,823 --> 00:30:25,824
Hey.

443
00:30:27,743 --> 00:30:29,703
A company is an organization, okay?

444
00:30:30,537 --> 00:30:34,249
Those above lead and pull
while those below support them.

445
00:30:34,624 --> 00:30:38,003
Laknes was my way of telling you
I'd take you with me.

446
00:30:38,462 --> 00:30:41,631
All you had to do was obey
and support me.

447
00:30:44,176 --> 00:30:45,719
I don't know that much yet.

448
00:30:45,802 --> 00:30:47,971
Maybe I'll understand
when I'm an associate director.

449
00:30:49,848 --> 00:30:51,850
You moron...

450
00:30:54,144 --> 00:30:55,896
Mr. Jang.

451
00:30:57,064 --> 00:30:58,648
Back in the day

452
00:30:59,358 --> 00:31:01,318
you argued with staff
at each brand's head office

453
00:31:02,486 --> 00:31:04,196
and sucked up to store staff.

454
00:31:05,280 --> 00:31:09,117
Despite all that,
you bought us soju to cheer us up.

455
00:31:10,619 --> 00:31:14,539
That's how great
a team leader you were.

456
00:31:17,292 --> 00:31:21,546
Can't I be a team leader like you?

457
00:31:26,676 --> 00:31:28,470
Did you get a job offer?

458
00:31:30,097 --> 00:31:32,474
You can be honest.

459
00:31:33,183 --> 00:31:34,184
You did.

460
00:31:34,267 --> 00:31:38,188
Either that, or you're doing this
because you have a Plan B.

461
00:31:38,897 --> 00:31:40,857
No? What is it, then?

462
00:31:41,525 --> 00:31:42,984
Did you win the lottery or something?

463
00:31:45,737 --> 00:31:46,863
Darn it.

464
00:32:04,256 --> 00:32:05,424
I got scared as hell.

465
00:32:22,732 --> 00:32:24,192
You sly thing.

466
00:32:28,405 --> 00:32:30,115
I can't stand you.

467
00:32:32,325 --> 00:32:35,370
- They should be done by now.
- Right?

468
00:32:36,079 --> 00:32:37,122
Hey, look.

469
00:32:43,670 --> 00:32:44,880
You didn't go home?

470
00:32:45,422 --> 00:32:46,840
Well...

471
00:32:48,425 --> 00:32:50,469
Were you afraid
I'd kill your team leader?

472
00:32:50,552 --> 00:32:52,429
Gosh, no.

473
00:32:53,096 --> 00:32:54,431
We're going out to dinner.

474
00:33:00,520 --> 00:33:02,856
You're a weird bunch.

475
00:33:03,690 --> 00:33:06,526
Just a few days ago,
you wanted to tear each other apart.

476
00:33:07,944 --> 00:33:09,738
- Here.
- No, thanks.

477
00:33:09,821 --> 00:33:11,364
Ms. Park gave me hers.

478
00:33:11,698 --> 00:33:13,074
I'll pay for the second round.

479
00:33:14,034 --> 00:33:15,702
Okay, then. Thank you.

480
00:33:17,370 --> 00:33:18,788
- Mr. Yang.
- Yes, sir.

481
00:33:19,664 --> 00:33:22,834
Your team leader loves beef so much
it'll wake him right up.

482
00:33:23,293 --> 00:33:25,086
- Have beef for dinner.
- Okay.

483
00:33:25,337 --> 00:33:27,047
- And go somewhere cheap for round 2.
- Got it.

484
00:33:28,256 --> 00:33:29,382
- Thank you.
- Bye, sir.

485
00:33:29,466 --> 00:33:30,592
Thank you.

486
00:33:37,557 --> 00:33:38,683
Hey, Eun-tae.

487
00:33:40,143 --> 00:33:41,394
Laknes...

488
00:33:42,270 --> 00:33:43,313
It'll do well.

489
00:33:44,147 --> 00:33:46,066
I wouldn't have given it to you
otherwise.

490
00:33:56,159 --> 00:33:57,202
Let's go.

491
00:33:57,619 --> 00:33:59,037
- Yes, sir.
- Okay.

492
00:34:26,940 --> 00:34:28,316
Do you know what to do?

493
00:34:34,990 --> 00:34:36,449
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

494
00:34:40,453 --> 00:34:42,038
Snap, snap.

495
00:35:06,146 --> 00:35:07,397
<i>You're embarrassed?</i>

496
00:35:08,398 --> 00:35:10,900
The other team leaders
are competing to get ahead.

497
00:35:11,401 --> 00:35:16,239
<i>Have you decided to do nothing
since you won't get promoted, anyway?</i>

498
00:35:24,372 --> 00:35:25,457
Good job, everyone.

499
00:35:25,540 --> 00:35:27,292
- You too.
- Good work.

500
00:35:31,171 --> 00:35:34,633
Mr. Gong, I feel awesome today.

501
00:35:35,383 --> 00:35:36,551
Why is that?

502
00:35:37,093 --> 00:35:38,303
It's like...

503
00:35:38,887 --> 00:35:42,724
I feel like I helped close this deal.

504
00:35:42,807 --> 00:35:44,017
That's why I feel good.

505
00:35:44,309 --> 00:35:47,812
I didn't actually do anything,
but that's how I feel.

506
00:35:47,896 --> 00:35:50,690
You're right. You didn't do anything.

507
00:35:50,982 --> 00:35:53,401
- What?
- We all did it together.

508
00:35:53,485 --> 00:35:55,195
Right, Mr. Gong?

509
00:35:55,278 --> 00:35:57,322
- See?
- Okay, let's go with that.

510
00:35:57,405 --> 00:35:58,490
"Let's go with that"?

511
00:36:00,241 --> 00:36:03,578
I appreciate Mr. Jang more now.

512
00:36:04,704 --> 00:36:05,747
How so?

513
00:36:06,373 --> 00:36:08,792
He said you liked beef

514
00:36:08,875 --> 00:36:10,669
and he gave us his corporate card.

515
00:36:11,086 --> 00:36:13,380
He also said Laknes would do well.

516
00:36:15,215 --> 00:36:16,549
He's like that.

517
00:36:16,966 --> 00:36:20,553
He knows exactly when to use
the carrot and the stick.

518
00:36:20,637 --> 00:36:23,098
It all worked out today, though.

519
00:36:23,181 --> 00:36:26,226
That's why I don't resent Mr. Jang

520
00:36:27,102 --> 00:36:28,645
even when he yells and curses me out.

521
00:36:28,728 --> 00:36:30,605
His praise means
just as little to me.

522
00:36:31,523 --> 00:36:35,443
I don't trust others enough
to let their words sway me.

523
00:36:38,196 --> 00:36:41,032
What do you believe in, then?

524
00:37:07,225 --> 00:37:08,268
<i>My past.</i>

525
00:37:14,357 --> 00:37:16,317
I believe in the life I've lived.

526
00:37:21,573 --> 00:37:23,533
That's so freaking cool.

527
00:37:24,117 --> 00:37:26,161
Can I quote that?

528
00:37:26,244 --> 00:37:27,829
No, don't you dare.

529
00:37:28,788 --> 00:37:31,416
"My past. I believe in the life..."

530
00:37:32,917 --> 00:37:35,086
Don't imitate me. It's embarrassing.

531
00:37:35,170 --> 00:37:36,337
Did I say it wrong?

532
00:37:36,421 --> 00:37:38,506
You shouldn't put so much faith
in your past.

533
00:37:38,590 --> 00:37:40,216
- That'll end badly.
- Why?

534
00:37:40,300 --> 00:37:41,634
- Can I try?
- Sure.

535
00:37:41,718 --> 00:37:44,637
"My past.
I believe in the life I've lived."

536
00:37:44,721 --> 00:37:46,347
- I said it better.
- Excuse me.

537
00:37:46,431 --> 00:37:48,641
You can't say it better than me.

538
00:37:48,725 --> 00:37:50,351
Say it properly, will you?

539
00:37:50,435 --> 00:37:52,061
"My past. I believe in my past."

540
00:37:52,145 --> 00:37:54,022
- Is that not right?
- You said it wrong.

541
00:37:54,647 --> 00:37:56,024
Why are you calling so late?

542
00:37:56,107 --> 00:37:58,193
The time is the least of our worries.

543
00:37:58,276 --> 00:38:00,570
The girl returning from China
is joining your team?

544
00:38:01,488 --> 00:38:02,489
Jang Hyang-eun.

545
00:38:02,822 --> 00:38:04,908
Jang Hyang-eun returns from China.

546
00:38:04,991 --> 00:38:06,701
Yes, she'll be back next week.

547
00:38:08,036 --> 00:38:09,245
Send her to Team 5.

548
00:38:10,038 --> 00:38:12,457
<i>Yes, she'll join my team. Why?</i>

549
00:38:12,832 --> 00:38:14,751
<i>You accepted her willingly?</i>

550
00:38:14,834 --> 00:38:17,420
<i>I did. She's good at her job.</i>

551
00:38:19,130 --> 00:38:22,926
Gong, I didn't mention this
because it's classified.

552
00:38:23,551 --> 00:38:25,553
The China branch is about to implode.

553
00:38:29,224 --> 00:38:30,308
What do you mean?

554
00:38:31,059 --> 00:38:33,436
<i>The branch was deeply corrupt.</i>

555
00:38:34,020 --> 00:38:38,024
<i>Word is, Jang Hyang-eun
was at the center of it all.</i>

556
00:38:39,025 --> 00:38:40,819
I think you picked the wrong person.

557
00:39:16,855 --> 00:39:21,776
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

558
00:39:34,163 --> 00:39:37,125
That's why your brand
ended up with our team.

559
00:39:37,584 --> 00:39:40,169
We're the weakest team.

560
00:39:41,170 --> 00:39:46,092
They expect us to do an average job
and give you what you want.

561
00:39:47,594 --> 00:39:54,559
You two expected to come here,
sign the deal, and move on.

562
00:39:55,894 --> 00:39:56,978
Am I wrong?

563
00:39:59,689 --> 00:40:01,190
Okay, next.

564
00:40:02,275 --> 00:40:04,819
<i>I'm sorry, but we have
no intention of doing that.</i>

565
00:40:04,903 --> 00:40:06,988
"I'm sorry, but we have..."

566
00:40:07,280 --> 00:40:10,283
<i>To you, Korea might be
just a stepping stone</i>

567
00:40:10,366 --> 00:40:13,578
<i>but to us, Laknes is a brand
we must build and grow.</i>

568
00:40:14,287 --> 00:40:16,122
<i>Adjust the margin.</i>

569
00:40:16,623 --> 00:40:18,249
<i>You'll make that much more.</i>

570
00:40:19,375 --> 00:40:21,127
<i>Are you that confident?</i>

571
00:40:22,128 --> 00:40:23,421
<i>You saw the numbers.</i>

572
00:40:25,924 --> 00:40:28,217
"You saw the numbers."

573
00:40:33,598 --> 00:40:34,849
You saw the numbers.

574
00:40:35,892 --> 00:40:37,352
That's not it.

575
00:40:38,394 --> 00:40:39,395
You saw the numbers.

576
00:40:39,479 --> 00:40:40,730
The numbers. You saw them.

577
00:40:40,813 --> 00:40:42,815
Hey, did you see this? The numbers.

578
00:40:42,899 --> 00:40:44,442
You saw the numbers, didn't you?

579
00:40:45,526 --> 00:40:46,694
You saw the num...

580
00:40:49,572 --> 00:40:50,907
Mr. Gong.

581
00:40:51,491 --> 00:40:52,533
Mr. Yang.

582
00:40:53,117 --> 00:40:54,118
Ji-hye?

583
00:41:06,214 --> 00:41:07,674
What the...

584
00:41:09,425 --> 00:41:11,052
That was so embarrassing.

585
00:43:41,410 --> 00:43:43,412
Subtitles by Jennifer Jean Lim

